<h1>Kids' Wing — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 25, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Kids' Wing (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.librarykids</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). This policy is written for parents and guardians. Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Kids' Wing collects <strong>no data at all</strong> — not from children, not from anyone. The app has <strong>no internet permission</strong>: it is technically incapable of connecting to the internet or sending anything anywhere. It works entirely offline. There are <strong>no ads, no in-app purchases, no accounts, no chat, and no external links in the children's area</strong>.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Stories and coloring, all on the device.</strong> The books (classic public-domain stories) and coloring pages are bundled inside the app. Reading and coloring happen on the device; nothing is transmitted, uploaded, or shared.</li>
  <li><strong>No personal information.</strong> The app never asks for a name, an email address, a photo, a location, or any other personal information, and it has no permission to access any.</li>
  <li><strong>The Parent Corner.</strong> A few text-only mentions for grown-ups (our other apps) sit behind a parent gate — a press-and-hold plus a simple arithmetic question. Even there, nothing is collected and no purchase happens inside the app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Nothing is collected or kept by us. Anything the app remembers — such as where a story left off — stays in the app on your own device. Uninstalling the app erases it.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>None.</strong> Kids' Wing requests zero Android permissions.</li>
  <li><strong>Internet: NOT requested.</strong> The app cannot connect to the internet.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads and purchases</h2>
<p>There are <strong>no ads</strong> in Kids' Wing and no advertising SDK of any kind. There are <strong>no in-app purchases</strong> offered to children; the children's area contains no shopping, no prices, and no links out.</p>

<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
<p>Because the app collects no personal information from anyone — including children under 13 — there is nothing to share, sell, or disclose. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children, and the app is built so that it cannot.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

